<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Hyundai Heavy wins $100 mln Israel order.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Hyundai Heavy wins $100 mln Israel order.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Hyundai Heavy Industries Co, a unit of the Hyundai Group, said on Tuesday it had won a $100 million port facility order from Israel Electric Corp (IEC).  </p>
<p>A company statement said the order was awarded on a turn-key basis.</p>
<p>It said the facility would be located at the port of Ashkelon in southern Israel. It would be used mainly for unloading coal which would be supplied to a thermal power plant in the area, it said.</p>
<p>The facility is scheduled to be completed by the end of 1999.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
